  {
    "description": "List the AI agents of the workspace with their prompt, model, role and triggers. System agents (those backing workflow AI steps or installed by an application) are not included.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "properties": {},
      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "list_agents",
  },
  {
    "description": "Create an AI agent that works on its own: it wakes up on its triggers (record events or a schedule) and acts with the tools its role allows, for example posting a note, updating records or sending a summary.

Before creating it, present the plan to the user (prompt, role, triggers) and get their confirmation, since the agent keeps running after this conversation.
Give the agent a role with the least access it needs (use list_roles to find one); without a role it cannot read or write records.
Write the prompt as standing instructions for every run, and put what to do for a specific trigger in that trigger's instructions.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "$defs": {
        "__schema0": {
          "description": "Id of an existing trigger, as returned by list_agents. Pass it to keep that trigger when updating; omit it for a new trigger.",
          "format": "uuid",
          "type": "string",
        },
        "__schema1": {
          "description": "Whether the trigger starts runs. Defaults to true.",
          "type": "boolean",
        },
        "__schema2": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "maxLength": 10000,
              "type": "string",
            },
            {
              "type": "null",
            },
          ],
          "description": "What the agent should do when this trigger fires, on top of its prompt (e.g. 'Post a summary of the new deal in a note on the company').",
        },
      },
      "properties": {
        "description": {
          "description": "Optional short description",
          "type": "string",
        },
        "icon": {
          "description": "Optional icon identifier (e.g. "IconRobot")",
          "type": "string",
        },
        "label": {
          "description": "Display name of the agent",
          "minLength": 1,
          "type": "string",
        },
        "modelId": {
          "description": "Model the agent runs on. Defaults to "workspace-default-model", the workspace default model.",
          "type": "string",
        },
        "prompt": {
          "description": "System prompt describing who the agent is and what it does on every run",
          "minLength": 1,
          "type": "string",
        },
        "roleId": {
          "description": "Role the agent acts with. Without a role the agent can neither read nor write any record.",
          "format": "uuid",
          "type": "string",
        },
        "triggers": {
          "description": "What wakes the agent up on its own. DATABASE_EVENT runs it when records change, with the changed records as input. CRON runs it on a schedule.",
          "items": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "properties": {
                  "id": {
                    "$ref": "#/$defs/__schema0",
